All five candidates verified against the actual code and server behavior.

```json
[
  {
    "id": "C1",
    "verdict": "CONFIRMED",
    "justification": "server/routes.ts:6777-6779 runs `quote = await storage.updateQuote(quote.id, { status: \"viewed\", viewedAt: new Date() }) ?? quote;` when status is 'sent' and returns that updated row in the same response, so the very first real-mode fetch delivers a non-null viewedAt; checkout.tsx:206-208 `if (quote?.viewedAt) setQuoteStep(\"confirm\")` then skips the 'view quote' step immediately. Mock returns `viewedAt: null` (mock-api buildMockQuote), which is why screenshots showed step 1."
  },
  {
    "id": "C2",
    "verdict": "CONFIRMED",
    "justification": "checkout.tsx:1209 reads exactly `onClick={() => { openQuotePdf(); if (quoteStep === \"view\") setQuoteStep(\"confirm\"); else respondToQuote(true); }}` — `openQuotePdf()` runs unconditionally, so tapping 'confirm' on step 2 pops a PDF tab (or trips the popup blocker) at the same moment the accept POST fires."
  },
  {
    "id": "C3",
    "verdict": "CONFIRMED",
    "justification": "respondToQuote's catch (checkout.tsx:238-239) only does `setQuoteRespondError((err as Error).message)` — no quote refetch and no invoice adoption — and the quote query is `retry: false`, so a 409 'Already responded' leaves the customer on the view/confirm card with an inline error and no path to the payment step. Minor nuance: the query keeps React Query's default `refetchOnWindowFocus`, so backgrounding and refocusing the tab would incidentally refetch and adopt `invoice.token`, but nothing in-tab recovers."
  },
  {
    "id": "C4",
    "verdict": "CONFIRMED",
    "justification": "The quote-phase terminal branch (checkout.tsx:1161-1162) only handles `status === \"declined\" || status === \"expired\"`; for an accepted quote whose invoices are all voided, routes.ts:6790-6792 `invoices.find((i) => i.status !== \"voided\")` yields no invoice so `invoice: null` is returned, acceptedInvoiceToken never gets set, the view/confirm UI renders, and confirming hits routes.ts:6773-6774 `if (quote.status === \"accepted\" ...) return res.status(409).json({ message: \"Already responded\" })` — a dead-end with no 'accepted' terminal state."
  },
  {
    "id": "C5",
    "verdict": "CONFIRMED",
    "justification": "public/sw.js:104-120 serves anything under `/assets/` cache-first-forever into STATIC_CACHE 'taptpay-static-v3' on the stated assumption that 'Vite build output is content-hashed', but non-hashed public files are served from the same prefix — client/public/assets/fonts/LarkenDEMO-*.otf and Outfit-*.otf exist and are referenced by checkout.css as `/assets/fonts/...` — and the activate handler (line 22) only deletes caches with *different names*, so a same-name replaced asset never reaches returning users until the cache name is bumped. client/public/sw.js is byte-identical (diff: IDENTICAL), so both copies carry the bug."
  }
]
```

Out-of-scope note: the network-first extension regex at sw.js:123 omits `otf` (has ttf/woff2 but not otf), so even outside `/assets/` an .otf would fall to the default handler — adjacent to C5 but not part of the verified claim.
